course: dictionary
lesson: 10981
title: Warmer: more heat, more kindness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Warmer» is a comparison word. It tells you one thing has more heat than another. Warm is the starting point, warmer is one step up, and warmest is the top. Look for what it is being compared to: if it is 15 °C today and 20 °C tomorrow, tomorrow is warmer.
explain: «Carbon dioxide in the air helps trap heat; more of it makes the Earth warmer.» Here warmer is about temperature: the Earth gets hotter. Ask yourself, warmer than what? The word «more» in the sentence is a clue that the Earth's temperature is going up.
explain: Warmer can also describe people. A warmer welcome is friendlier and kinder than a cold one. And warmer can name a thing that keeps you warm, like a leg warmer. Use the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Warmer is the comparative of warm: warm, warmer, warmest.
fact: «Warmer» means having a higher temperature than something else.
fact: «Warmer» can mean friendlier or kinder, as in a warmer welcome.
fact: A warmer is a thing that keeps something warm, like a hand warmer.
fact: In a hiding game, «warmer!» means you are getting closer to the hidden thing, and «colder» means further away.
exercise: Today is 15 °C and tomorrow is 20 °C. Is tomorrow warmer or colder? | *Warmer | Just the same | Wetter | Colder
exercise: «Carbon dioxide in the air helps trap heat; more of it makes the Earth warmer.» What does warmer mean here? | Having more clouds | Shinier | *Having a higher temperature | Friendlier to people
exercise: Sam is hiding and his friend shouts, «Warmer!» What does that tell Sam? | You have been found | *You are getting closer to the hidden thing | You are going further away | The game is over
test: Which word is the comparative of warm? | *warmer | warmest | warming | warmth
test: The teacher gave the new pupil a warmer welcome. What does warmer mean here? | Wetter and greyer | Louder and busier | *Friendlier and kinder | Hotter than before
exam: Which is a warmer, a thing that keeps something warm? | A warm day | A cold drink | A window | *A hand warmer
